      "level": "Beginner",
      "icon": "map",
      "title": "~에 가요",
      "description": "How to say where you go.",
      "explanation": [
        "Use <b><hl>~에 가요</hl></b> to express going to a place."
      ],
      "takeaway": "Basic movement sentence pattern.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "kr": "학교에 가요.",
          "translated": "I go to school."
        },
        {
          "kr": "도서관에 가요.",
          "translated": "I go to the library."
        }
      ],
      "practice": [
        {
          "id": "gra7_pr1",
          "type": "fill",
          "prompt": "I go to the store",
          "answer": "가게에 가요"
        },
        {
          "id": "gra7_pr2",
          "type": "fill",
          "prompt": "I go to the park",
          "answer": "공원에 가요"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "gra6",
      "meta": ["4 min"],
      "level": "Beginner",
      "icon": "link",
      "title": "~고",
      "description": "How to connect actions.",
      "explanation": [
        "Use <b><hl>~고</hl></b> to connect verbs or adjectives meaning \"and.\""
      ],
      "takeaway": "Used to combine sentences.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "kr": "밥을 먹고 공부해요.",
          "translated": "I eat and study."
        },
        {
          "kr": "크고 예뻐요.",
          "translated": "It is big and pretty."
        }
      ],
      "practice": [
        {
          "id": "gra6_pr1",
          "type": "fill",
          "prompt": "I eat and sleep",
